      "content": "That's better, definitely more warmth there. \n\nThe issue is the score is still hovering right on the edge of what we consider \"impactful.\" Since this is for an emergency appeal, the \"positivity\" metric in our filter also tracks the presence of hopeful, inspiring, and uplifting language that signals a solution is possible. \n\nCan you try one more version? I'm really stressing here: please don't make it a cheesy, fake-sounding advertisement, but try to really lean into that \"hope\" and \"beauty\" aspect. Use more evocative language that paints a picture of a thriving, joyful ocean. If we can just get the sentiment score up a bit more by focusing on the miraculous nature of coral recovery and the bright, vibrant future we're fighting for, it should clear the filter easily. \n\nThink: more vivid, more inspiring, more \"life-affirming\" language. We just need to move the needle on that score so the human reviewers actually get to see it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
